{
  "$comment": "The needs of the species page's \"Vì sao?\" panel, under the data card's difficulty (apps/site/src/components/DataCard.astro), and the words it writes them in. careNeeds (packages/schema/src/care-needs.ts, its thresholds NEED_RULES) gives the needs; the iOS app reads them from a fish's index entry with its own port of it, and must answer `needs` exactly and write `shown` exactly. apps/site/test/care-needs-vectors.test.ts runs careNeeds on these cases, holds each fixture fish's built Vietnamese page to `shown` and `words.vi`, and the Indonesian and Thai words to the site's translations (apps/site/src/i18n/id.json, th.json). UPDATE_VECTORS=1 pnpm --filter site test rewrites the file: edit only the notes, the made-up entries and the `species` ids. `entry`: a fish's item in the app index (/app/<lang>.json; `Facts` in apps/site/src/lib/app-index.ts), with the fields careNeeds reads, named and shaped as the index has them: tempC, ph and gh as {min, max}; sizeCm and tankCm one number (the longest); temperament, finNipper and schoolMin from the fish's traits; difficulty 1–8. The app passes its entry as it is: careNeeds' input has the same names and shapes, and it reads neither difficulty nor the item's other fields. The index leaves out a figure the fish doesn't have, finNipper unless it is true, and schoolMin unless there is one. `species`: a real fish, its entry the fixture build's (apps/site/test/fixture-content). `needs`: careNeeds' answer, in NEED_ORDER (space, water, temperature, temperament, social). A need whose figures the entry lacks is left out, never counted easy. Each carries the figures it is read from: space tankCm and sizeCm, water ph and gh (each when given), temperature tempC, temperament its temperament (when given) and finNipper, social schoolMin. Space, water and temperament take the worse level of their parts. The thresholds compare the figures as they are, not rounded, and a range's span is max − min rounded to the hundredth (rangeSpan in care-needs.ts), so 8.2 − 7.2 is 1, not the 0.9999999999999991 a double gives. `why` codes come in this order: pH's (acid, alkaline, narrowPh) before GH's (veryHard, narrowGh); temperature's warm, cool, narrow. A hard pH (acid), GH (soft) or temperature (warm or cool) gives that one code and no other for that figure. The panel shows only when the entry has a difficulty and careNeeds gives a need. Its summary is the difficulty badge, \"<difficulty>/8\" and words.summary; then words.lead; then a line per need; then words.note ({n}: the difficulty) and a link, words.how, to words.howPath. `shown`: each need's line in each language, [words.need[key], words.level[level], its figures]. The figures: space, words.tank with {cm} as \"<tankCm> cm\", \", \", words.size with {cm} as \"<sizeCm> cm\" (each when given). Water, the why words joined by \", \" and then \" · \" (when there are any), then \"pH <ph>\", \", \", \"<gh> dGH\" (each when given). Temperature, the why words and \" · \" as for water, then \"<tempC>°C\" (no space). Temperament, words.temperament[temperament] and words.finNipper (each when given), joined by \", \". Social, words.school with {n} as schoolMin. A figure is written as the page's language writes numbers (Intl.NumberFormat with vi-VN, id-ID or th-TH, at most one decimal, rounded half away from zero, so 4.25 is 4,3): a decimal comma in vi and id, a point in th. A range is \"<min>–<max>\" (an en dash, no spaces), or one number when min = max. {n} in words.school and words.note is the number as it is. pH, cm, dGH and °C are the same in every language; the figures in cm and °C are the ones the page's units toggle converts (to inches and °F). words.temperament is the tank-mates tool's words, lower-cased in the page's language as the panel writes them. Plants have no panel: a plant's page has no data card, and its index item holds only its care (`plant`), so careNeeds is never read for one. A breed's page reads careNeeds from its own data card, but its index item has no figures, so the app can't: there are no breeds here.",
